<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Menéndez de Avilés</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1519–1574</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Menéndez de Avilés was a Spanish admiral who founded St. Augustine in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> in 1565, the oldest continuously inhabited European settlement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. In the same year he destroyed the French Huguenot colony at Fort Caroline and executed most of its men. As governor of Spanish Florida he made alliances and conflicts with peoples such as the Calusa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-menendez-de-aviles.jpg" alt="Pedro Menéndez de Avilés" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Camarón y Boronat (1730-1803), published by Fran(cis)co de Paula Marti in 1791 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_menendez_de_Aviles.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
